{"records":[{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gfcn2wmrpf","title":"Dataset for the paper entitled \"A genetic map of the response to DNA damage in human cells\" by Olivieri M et al. Cell 2020","description":"We used pooled CRISPR/Cas9 screens in the human RPE1-hTERT p53-/- cell line against 27 genotoxic agents. The Dataset herein make the primary data available. The files are:\n\n* Additional genes of interest (discussion and data relating to TMEM2, ESD, USP37, PHF12, BTAF1 and DRAP1)\n* Supplementary Raw Data: Data used to make all the graphs in the manuscript\n* Folder \"CRISPR screen readcount files\". Readcounts for the screens undertaken as part of this study.\n* Folder \"Raw images for immunoblots\": uncropped images for all the blots in the manuscript\n* Folder: \"Additional QC analyses of CRISPR screens\": Additional analyses that measure the quality of the screens using Presion-Recall curves of essential genes and an estimate of genes that scored as hits due to batch effects.\n* Folder \"Data_Analysis_Code\" R markdown file along with data files\n* File: \"Additional Genes of Interests\" contains a short discussion of genes we found noteworthy after analysis of our screen data.\n\nVersion 2 note: this version differs from Version 1 by a single file (FDRPos_31screens.csv) which has a tab error fixed.\n\n\n\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-07-07T14:26:40.176Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gfcn2wmrpf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gfcn2wmrpf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Daniel","last_name":"Durocher","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michele","last_name":"Olivieri","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Data Quality","Primary Data"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"88xx6596wz","title":"cxt_bcWNV_amplicon_seq","description":"Amplicon sequencing of a molecular barcode in the NS4b coding region of the West Nile virus genome. Viral RNA extracted from Cx. tarsalis mosquitoes. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-02T20:53:29.119Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/88xx6596wz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/88xx6596wz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Emily","last_name":"Fitzmeyer","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"s7kthpysb7","title":"cxq_bcWNV_amplicon_seq","description":"Amplicon sequencing of a molecular barcode in the NS4b coding region of the West Nile virus genome. Viral RNA extracted from Cx. quinquefasciatus mosquitoes. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-02T20:50:42.145Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s7kthpysb7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s7kthpysb7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Emily","last_name":"Fitzmeyer","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"y6xjbjcgz8","title":"Docking of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus surface antigen with SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody","description":"Docking of SARS-CoV-2 Spike antibody with surface antigen of Dengue virus type 1 or West Nile Virus using ClusPro and ZDOCK","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-09T09:56:09.616Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y6xjbjcgz8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y6xjbjcgz8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Subhajit","last_name":"Biswas","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology","West Nile Virus","Dengue Virus","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"556zktntym","title":"aea_bcWNV_amplicon_seq","description":"Amplicon sequencing of a molecular barcode in the NS4b coding region of the West Nile virus genome. Viral RNA extracted from Ae. aegypti mosquitoes. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-02T20:49:18.969Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/556zktntym","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/556zktntym"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Emily","last_name":"Fitzmeyer","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vj6y364h79","title":"Exposure of negative-sense viral RNA in the cytoplasm initiates innate immunity to West Nile virus. Genoyer, et al.","description":"Raw data files associated with Genoyer, et al. 2025 manuscript describing negative-sense viral RNA driven innate immune activation during West Nile virus infection.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-27T08:13:49.424Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vj6y364h79","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vj6y364h79"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Michael","la